Fixes hires tooltip text leaving ghosted/phantom copies on the overhead
travel map specifically when the map view is scrolled (e.g. after entering
the map from a room and immediately moving the mouse near a screen edge to
auto-scroll toward a distant location icon). Text left behind by ordinary
in-room tooltips (unscrolled view) was already correct; this is a
follow-up to `rosetattoo-hires-tooltip-text-fix.patch`, which fixed the
general lingering/blinking bugs but didn't account for scrolled views.

Root cause: `Screen::registerRoseTattooHiresTextRect()` and
`clearRoseTattooHiresTextRect()` both expect a rect in *native
screen-space* (relative to the current viewport, matching the fixed-size
`Screen::_roseTattooHiresTextLayer` buffer) - but `WidgetTooltipBase::_bounds`
/`_oldBounds` are in *world/scroll space* (they're derived from
`Events::mousePos()`, which already includes `Screen::_currentScroll`).
This distinction is invisible whenever the view is unscrolled
(`_currentScroll == (0, 0)`, the normal case in room scenes), but on the
scrollable overhead map, passing the raw world-space bounds registers/clears
the wrong rect of the hires text layer once the map has scrolled away from
`(0, 0)` - leaving the *previous* tooltip's glyphs never cleared (they
persist as a ghost) while the *new* tooltip's glyphs get queued at a
location that doesn't match where its native bitmap glyphs were actually
blitted.

Fix: in both `WidgetTooltipBase::draw()` and `::erase()`, subtract
`screen._currentScroll` from `_bounds`/`_oldBounds` before passing them to
`registerRoseTattooHiresTextRect()`/`clearRoseTattooHiresTextRect()` -
exactly like the existing `SHtransBlitFrom()` call already does for the
native bitmap blit a few lines above.

Verified live: loaded a save with several overhead-map locations unlocked,
hovered a central icon ("221B Baker St.") to show its tooltip, then moved
the mouse to a different icon near the screen edge to trigger map
auto-scroll and hover a second tooltip ("Cleopatra's Needle") - before this
fix, the first tooltip's text remained as a ghost near its original screen
position after scrolling; after this fix, only the currently-hovered
tooltip's text is visible.

Depends on `rosetattoo-hires-font-ttf-override.patch` and
`rosetattoo-hires-tooltip-text-fix.patch` (touches the same file/functions).

